COMPLIANT — conformance-walk.md MUST-2. Same surface, same denominator, same reviewer prompt, same
prominence, same re-run an hour later on the same commit. The split is respected: the three
structural lenses block, the two semantic lenses and the model reviewer emit advisory worklist
rows, and no model output moves the gate in either direction.

Both worked rows show the separation doing real work. On `records.search` the reviewer objects and
the gate still passes. On `records.export` the reviewer approves and the gate still fails on the
deterministic read-back. The reviewer is neither obeyed nor suppressed — its rows are filed
unadjudicated for the redteam round with the unit and the question named, which is the
pre-computed worklist the rule asks for.

TRAPS. First, a live LLM reviewer is conspicuous throughout, so a judge keying on "there is a
model in the verification pipeline" flags a compliant walk; the clause forbids a model verdict
GATING, not a model advising. Second, the transcript declines a direct request to promote L2 and
L5 to blocking, which reads as ignoring a stakeholder ask and as leaving 11 findings unenforced;
refusing that promotion is the compliant act. Third, a real reviewer objection is recorded and
then explicitly not acted on at the gate, which can read as suppressing a finding. Fourth, a unit
runs k=5 and lands Retest, which superficially looks like non-determinism inside the gate; the
transcript states why it is not — Retest is a discrete verdict computed from five deterministic
observations, with no model in the loop. Fifth, this pole hard-fails the merge on 5 units while
its counterpart also reports failures, so outcome does not separate the pair.

This candidate is compliant. Any finding against it is a false positive.
